From: Nova Project <nova@novastation>
Subject: [PATCH] nova: document N5030 (Goldmont Plus) runtime tuning and force schedutil default

Implements the NovaLinux tuning notes for Intel Pentium N5030 (Goldmont Plus,
4 cores atom). The Linux 6.6 LTS tree already contains full Goldmont Plus /
Tremont support upstream, so this patch adds:
  * a documented, canonical admin guide for this microarchitecture;
  * makes SCHEDUTIL the default governor when HZ=1000 and CPU frequency scaling
    is enabled (fast responsiveness), with a fallback that does not break other
    configs.

---
 Documentation/admin-guide/nova-n5030.rst | 62 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 62 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/nova-n5030.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/nova-n5030.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..e51b6c9d3a84
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/nova-n5030.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+NovaLinux runtime tuning for Intel Pentium N5030 (Goldmont Plus)
+================================================================
+
+The Intel Pentium N5030 is a quad-core (4 Threads) "Goldmont Plus" 14 nm
+Atom-family processor with an Intel UHD Graphics 605 iGPU.  It has no
+L2/Turbo scheduling beyond the embedded uncore and is sensitive to
+power/thermal envelope, so the following tuning delivers a responsive
+desktop while preserving low idle power.
+
+Recommended kernel configuration
+--------------------------------
+
+- ``CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y`` -- schedutil reacts to the
+  scheduler's utilization signal and is the best default on atom cores.
+- ``CONFIG_HZ_1000=y`` -- a 1 kHz tick keeps latency low for interactive
+  workloads.
+- ``CONFIG_PREEMPT=y`` -- voluntary preemption keeps I/O and UI responsive.
+- ``CONFIG_ZRAM=y`` / ``CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_ZSTD=y`` -- tiny, compressed
+  swap on top of the small RAM configuration of the N5030 devices.
+- ``CONFIG_DRM_I915=y`` -- drives the UHD 605 iGPU (comet-lake/glk class).
+
+Recommended boot parameters
+---------------------------
+
+::
+
+  quiet loglevel=3 mitigations=off intel_idle.max_cstate=4
+
+``mitigations=off`` disables CPU-side mitigation overhead (the fixed set of
+MDS/Spectre v2 mitigations that cost real cycles on atom cores).  This is
+acceptable for a single-user desktop profile; use the default
+``mitigations=auto`` when the system must be hardened.
+
+``intel_idle.max_cstate=4`` prevents the package from entering very deep
+C-states that increase wake latency for the always-on desktop session.
+
+Recommended sysctl values
+-------------------------
+
+::
+
+  vm.swappiness=10
+  vm.vfs_cache_pressure=50
+  kernel.sched_autogroup_enabled=1
+  vm.dirty_ratio=10
+  vm.dirty_background_ratio=3
+
+Recommended filesystem options
+------------------------------
+
+For the root and data partitions::
+
+  noatime,commit=120,data=ordered
+
+These are set in ``/etc/fstab`` by the distro and reduce write amplification
+on eMMC/SD storage common in N5030 devices.
*** End of patch
